<title>USA: Reserve unveils convertible fund.</title>
<headline>Reserve unveils convertible fund.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reserve Funds said it launched the Reserve Convertible Securities fund, a domestic equity fund that seeks both capital appreciation and current income.</p>
<p>The fund will specialize in convertible preferred shares, which offer a fixed rate of income likes bonds and convert into common shares.</p>
<p>Reserve Funds has 11 money market funds with $3 billion in assets under management, as well as seven equity funds.</p>
